// Title: Uncommon Sigverif.EXE Child Process
// Sigma ID: 7d4aaec2-08ed-4430-8b96-28420e030e04
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-19 | Modified: 2024-08-27
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1216
// Description: Detects uncommon child processes spawning from "sigverif.exe", which could indicate potential
//   abuse of the latter as a living of the land binary in order to proxy execution.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.hexacorn.com/blog/2018/04/27/i-shot-the-sigverif-exe-the-gui-based-lolbin/
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1457676633809330184
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sigverif_uncommon_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\sigverif.exe" and (not((FolderPath in~ ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\WerFault.exe", "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\WerFault.exe"))))
